@startuml
title FST-037 - Project and review distraction history
autonumber
participant "Distraction worker" as Worker
participant "Transactional projection" as Project
participant "Outbox + ledger + log" as DB
actor Learner
participant "Distractions page" as UI
participant "Authenticated log query" as Query
Worker -> DB : read bounded pending distraction event IDs
loop each event, independent transaction
  Worker -> Project : project(eventId)
  Project -> DB : lock projection; read committed source
  Project -> Project : validate version and immutable target facts
  Project -> DB : insert receipt/event if absent
  Project -> DB : load correlated detection + outcomes
  Project -> Project : validate facts and chronology; choose deterministic outcome
  alt detection present
    Project -> DB : update derived log
  else outcome arrived first
    note right of Project : Keep ledger entry; no invented detection.
  end
  Project -> DB : mark source delivered and commit atomically
end
Learner -> UI : review history / apply session and date filters
UI -> Query : GET /api/v1/distractions?sessionId=&from=&to=&page=&size=
Query -> Query : validate filters and local-date UTC bounds
Query -> DB : count + stable paginated read
DB --> Query : immutable snapshots and confirmed/pending/failed outcomes
Query --> UI : 200 { items, total, page, size }
UI --> Learner : target, time, action and truthful outcome
note over Project, UI
  Projection/replay never invokes OS/browser enforcement.
  Rule edits cannot change saved detection snapshots.
  Session cleanup cascades ledger/log rows; late writes require a live session.
end note
@enduml
